5]},{"tree":[62,38,14,5]}],"notes":"Tadao Ando's Langen Foundation (2004) on the former missile station by Hombroich. Refined 6 Oct 2026 from published descriptions (the foundation's and baukunst-nrw's dimensions) and the OpenStreetMap outlines in the ground file, not photographs. The ground shows the long building east-west north of the museum's point, the water basin south-east of its east end, and the two wings running south-east at 45 degrees; the old model's long building stood about 5 m too far north and its wings about 10 m too far west, so both were moved onto the outlines and the whole rebuilt with rotated parts instead of rasterised rows. The long building: the concrete core, 76 x 10.8 x 6 m, inside its glass envelope (82 x 16 x 7.6 m) with steel posts and girders and a glass roof, on a low concrete plinth, the door at the core's west end. The basin with its concrete edges, and the guiding concrete wall that leads along it to the door; a gravel approach to the north. The wings: two parallel concrete halls 44 m long and 9 m wide, sunk six metres so only 3.45 m stands, each with a roof light, the sunken walk between them reached by a stair, low earth banks (dry grass) along their outer sides; trees of the old station's woods at the edges. Still guessed: the wings' length and spacing, the banks, the basin's exact outline, the envelope's mullion rhythm."}